Goal: one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test that adds a new workspace packages/jsonl-lint and meets every acceptance line of issue https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102. Context: packages/ does not exist yet; the root package.json already declares workspaces packages/* and its test script runs `npm test --workspaces --if-present`; CI (.github/workflows/test.yml) runs `npm ci` then `npm test` on Node 22. Follow CLAUDE.md: Node 22+, plain ES modules, zero runtime dependencies, no build step, node:test.

Steps:
1. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json with "name": "jsonl-lint", "type": "module", "scripts": { "test": "node --test" }, a "bin": { "jsonl-lint": "bin/jsonl-lint.js" } entry, and no "dependencies" (no devDependencies needed either). Optionally "private": true and "engines": { "node": ">=22" }.
2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exporting `lint(text)` that returns an array of `{ line, error }` objects, one per row that is not valid JSON. Split text on "\n" (strip a trailing "\r" per row), number lines 1-based, skip rows that are blank or whitespace-only, and JSON.parse every other row including a final row with no trailing newline (an unterminated/torn last line must be checked, not dropped). `error` is the parse error message string. A trailing newline at end of file must not produce an extra error. Return [] for clean input.
3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js (shebang `#!/usr/bin/env node`, executable bit set via `git update-index --chmod=+x` or chmod before commit). Usage: `jsonl-lint <file>`. With no argument, or if the file cannot be read (missing), print a message to stderr and exit 2. Otherwise read the file as UTF-8, call lint, print one line per error to stdout in the exact form `<file>:<line>: <error>` where <file> is the argument as given, and exit 1 if there were any errors, 0 if none. Import lint relative to the bin file (new URL / import from '../src/index.js').
4. Add node:test tests under packages/jsonl-lint/test/ (e.g. test/lint.test.js and test/cli.test.js; `node --test` with no args discovers files matching *.test.js under test/). Cover at least: a clean file (no errors, CLI exit 0); a bad middle row (error reported at the correct 1-based line, CLI prints `<file>:<line>: ...` and exits 1); a torn last row with no trailing newline (reported); blank lines (skipped, and line numbers of later rows stay correct); and the exit codes 0, 1, and 2 for both a missing file and no argument (check stderr is non-empty and stdout empty for exit 2). Run the CLI with child_process spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, ...]) and write fixtures to a temp dir (fs.mkdtempSync(os.tmpdir())).
5. Create packages/jsonl-lint/README.md describing purpose, usage (`node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>`), output format, exit codes 0/1/2, and the lint(text) API.
6. Update the root README.md: replace the "No tools yet" bullet under "What is here" with an entry listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and a one-line description.
7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so package-lock.json records the new workspace, and commit the updated package-lock.json; then confirm `npm ci` and `npm test` both succeed from the root (CI uses npm ci, which fails if the lock file is out of sync).
8. Open one PR whose body contains the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the test workflow to finish on the PR head and make sure it is green; if it fails, fix and push to the same PR until it passes.